  "prompt": "Evaluate $$\\int_0^{\\pi/4}\\frac{2\\tan\\theta}{1+\\tan^2\\theta}\\,d\\theta.$$",
  "image": null,
  "choices": null,
  "answer": "1/2",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Trig identity",
    "body": "Since $1+\\tan^2\\theta=\\sec^2\\theta$, the integrand is $2\\tan\\theta\\cos^2\\theta=2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta=\\sin2\\theta$. Then $\\int_0^{\\pi/4}\\sin2\\theta\\,d\\theta=\\left[-\\frac{\\cos2\\theta}2\\right]_0^{\\pi/4}=0+\\frac12=\\frac12$.\n\n**Answer: $\\frac12$**"
   }
  ],
  "topics": [
