  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Substitute $u=x^2$",
    "body": "With $u=x^2$, $du=2x\\,dx$ and the upper limit becomes $2^{-1/2}$, so the integral is $\\int_0^{1/\\sqrt2}\\frac{du}{\\sqrt{1-u^2}}=\\arcsin\\frac1{\\sqrt2}=\\frac\\pi4$.\n\n**Answer: $\\frac\\pi4$**"
   }
  ],
