  "prompt": "Evaluate $$\\int_0^1\\cfrac{1}{1+\\cfrac{1}{1+\\cfrac1x}}\\,dx.$$",
  "image": null,
  "choices": null,
  "answer": "1/2+ln(3)/4",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "answerDisplay": "$\\frac12\\left(1+\\frac{\\ln 3}{2}\\right)$",
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Simplify the continued fraction",
    "body": "$1+\\frac1x=\\frac{x+1}x$, so $\\frac1{1+1/x}=\\frac x{x+1}$. Then $1+\\frac x{x+1}=\\frac{2x+1}{x+1}$ and the integrand is $\\frac{x+1}{2x+1}=\\frac12+\\frac1{2(2x+1)}$.\n\nIntegrating from $0$ to $1$: $\\frac12+\\frac14\\ln(2x+1)\\Big|_0^1=\\frac12+\\frac{\\ln3}4=\\frac12\\left(1+\\frac{\\ln3}2\\right)$.\n\n**Answer: $\\frac12+\\frac{\\ln3}4$**"
   }
  ],
  "topics": [
