  "prompt": "Evaluate $$\\int_1^2\\frac{x^3+x^{-3}}{x^1+x^{-1}}\\,dx.$$",
  "image": null,
  "choices": null,
  "answer": "11/6",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Sum of cubes",
    "body": "With $s=x+x^{-1}$, $s^3=x^3+3x+3x^{-1}+x^{-3}$, so $x^3+x^{-3}=s^3-3s$ and the integrand is $s^2-3=x^2+x^{-2}-1$. Then $\\int_1^2\\left(x^2+x^{-2}-1\\right)dx=\\left[\\frac{x^3}3-\\frac1x-x\\right]_1^2=\\left(\\frac83-\\frac12-2\\right)-\\left(\\frac13-1-1\\right)=\\frac{11}6$.\n\n**Answer: $\\frac{11}6$**"
   }
  ],
  "topics": [
   "calculus"
  ],
  "difficulty": 2,
  "duplicateOf": null,
  "reviewNote": null
 },
