   {
    "title": "Reverse product rule",
    "body": "Seek $g$ with $g+g'=\\tan x+\\tan^2x-x=(\\tan x-x)+(\\sec^2x-1)$. Taking $g=\\tan x-x$ gives $g'=\\sec^2x-1$, so the integrand is $\\left(e^x(\\tan x-x)\\right)'$. The value is $e(\\tan1-1)-0$.\n\n**Answer: $e(\\tan1-1)$**"
   }
