  "type": "numeric",
  "prompt": "Evaluate $$\\int_0^{\\pi/4}\\tan^2(2\\theta-1)\\,d\\theta.$$",
  "image": null,
  "choices": null,
  "answer": "1/sin(2)-pi/4",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "answerDisplay": "$\\csc 2-\\frac{\\pi}{4}$",
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Substitute and use $\\tan^2=\\sec^2-1$",
    "body": "With $u=2\\theta-1$: $\\frac12\\int_{-1}^{\\pi/2-1}\\tan^2u\\,du=\\frac12\\left[\\tan u-u\\right]_{-1}^{\\pi/2-1}$. Using $\\tan\\left(\\frac\\pi2-1\\right)=\\cot1$, this is $\\frac12\\left[\\left(\\cot1-\\frac\\pi2+1\\right)-(-\\tan1+1)\\right]=\\frac12\\left[\\cot1+\\tan1-\\frac\\pi2\\right]$. Since $\\cot1+\\tan1=\\frac1{\\sin1\\cos1}=\\frac2{\\sin2}$, the value is $\\frac1{\\sin2}-\\frac\\pi4=\\csc2-\\frac\\pi4$.\n\n**Answer: $\\csc2-\\frac\\pi4$**"
   }
  ],
  "topics": [
